  "parent": {
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What your child is learning",
        "text": "Two ways to multiply by 6. Because 6 = 5 + 1, a 6s fact is the 5s fact plus one more group: 6 × 7 = 5 × 7 + 1 × 7 = 35 + 7 = 42. Because 6 = 3 + 3, it is also double the 3s fact: 3 × 7 + 3 × 7 = 21 + 21 = 42. Both are the Distributive Property."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Try it with real things",
        "list": [
          "Lay out 6 rows of 7 buttons. Cover the bottom row: 5 rows is 35. Uncover it: 35 + 7 = 42.",
          "Now cover the bottom 3 rows: 21 buttons. Uncover them: 21 + 21 = 42."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Questions to ask",
        "list": [
          "Where is the 6?",
          "What is the 5s fact? What is one more group?",
          "What is the 3s fact? What is double that?"
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Common mistakes",
        "list": [
          "Adding 1 instead of one more group: 35 + 1 instead of 35 + 7.",
          "Stopping at the 5s fact.",
          "Breaking 6 into numbers that do not add up to 6, such as 3 and 2.",
          "Adding the factors: 6 + 7 = 13."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "A note on notation",
        "text": "Some books write the facts without ( ) and some with ( ). Both mean the same thing. Study Scoop uses original practice questions; it never copies the textbook."
      }
    ]
  }
